+# Public application API v1
+
+Implementation-level HTTP reference for an external application (e.g. STIR) integrating osTRIS.
+This is **not** protocol specification - it exposes normative concepts already defined in
+`CORE_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md`/`CORE_WIRE_AND_DECISION_SEMANTICS_V0_1.md` through clean read/provisioning
+endpoints. Where this document and those disagree on economic/cryptographic semantics, the
+normative specs govern.
+
+All endpoints require an authenticated IDAX request in the target tenant (the same bearer token
+used against any other module in the instance) and enforce tenant isolation via RLS plus explicit
+tenant-scoped queries, matching every other osTRIS endpoint.
+
+## Discovery (`OSTRIS_DISCOVERY_READ`, `OSTRIS_TRANSACTION_READ`)
+
+| Method | Path | Returns |
+|---|---|---|
+| GET | `/api/ostris/communities` | Communities in the caller's tenant |
+| GET | `/api/ostris/communities/{community}` | One community |
+| GET | `/api/ostris/communities/{community}/units` | Units of account in the community |
+| GET | `/api/ostris/communities/{community}/units/{unit}` | One unit (`code`, `scale`) |
+| GET | `/api/ostris/communities/{community}/accounts/{account}` | Account: `unitId`, `participantId`, `accountType`, `creditFloor`, `balanceProjection`, `riskState` |
+| GET | `/api/ostris/communities/{community}/credentials/{credential}` | Credential: public key, algorithm, activation/revocation sequence, bound `controllerId` |
+| GET | `/api/ostris/transactions/{id}` | Transaction status/signing/receipt (below) |
+
+`GET /api/ostris/transactions/{id}` is the one endpoint a client needs both **before** and
+**after** signing:
+
+```json
+{
+  "transactionId": "...", "communityId": "...", "unitId": "...", "purpose": "EXCHANGE",
+  "wireFormat": "OSTRIS-CORE-JCS-1", "ostrisCoreVersion": "0.1",
+  "authorizationPayload": "<exact canonical JCS UTF-8 text stored at propose() time>",
+  "authorizationDigest": "<sha256 hex of OSTRIS:TX:AUTH:V1 || 0x00 || authorizationPayload bytes>",
+  "status": "PROPOSED | COMMITTED",
+  "committedSequence": null, "protocolDigest": null,
+  "authorizedAccountIds": ["..."]
+}
+```
+
+A client never reconstructs `AuthorizationPayload` itself. It fetches this exact `authorizationPayload`
+string, builds the signing bytes as `UTF8("OSTRIS:TX:AUTH:V1") || 0x00 || UTF8(authorizationPayload)`,
+signs those bytes with the account's Ed25519 credential, and POSTs the resulting
+`signatureBase64url` to `POST /api/ostris/transactions/{id}/authorizations` (unchanged, see
+`TransactionController`). `status` never becomes `"REJECTED"`: a failed `commit()` call throws
+synchronously (the caller learns rejection from that HTTP error) and the proposal simply stays
+`PROPOSED` forever - polling this endpoint is for reconciling a client that lost the commit
+response, not for discovering rejection.
+
+## Provisioning (`OSTRIS_COMMUNITY_MANAGE`, `OSTRIS_PARTICIPANT_ACTIVATE`)
+
+| Method | Path | Body | Creates |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| POST | `/api/ostris/communities` | `{name}` | Community |
+| POST | `/api/ostris/communities/{community}/units` | `{code, scale}` | Unit of account |
+| POST | `/api/ostris/communities/{community}/participants/activate` | `{displayName, unitId, publicKeyBase64url, creditFloor?}` | Participant + Account + Credential + Controller + binding + 1-of-1 AccountControlPolicy |
+
+`activate` is the one call an application needs per user: it provisions exactly what
+`TransactionalAuthorizationPostgresTest`'s fixtures already built by hand (see that file), using
+`UuidV7` identifiers and `activation_sequence = 0` (active before any transaction commits, same as
+those fixtures). `publicKeyBase64url` is the caller's own already-generated Ed25519 public key -
+osTRIS never generates, sees or stores a private key. `creditFloor` defaults to `-100000` minor
+units and must be `<= 0`.
+
+Multi-credential rotation, RiskSubject/IdentityAssurance enrollment and governed multi-controller
+authorities remain out of this MVP surface; they provision directly against the normative tables
+(as today) or a future richer endpoint - this is intentionally the minimal path to one working,
+signable, committable account per participant.
